7:interfaces: "P2.1 env-readiness-FSM child c1 (`fsm_detect`) — the FIRST env state (DETECT), built on the LANDED c0 shared contract `ngv2/fsm_evidence.py` (commit dc07188: `phase_artifact_hash`, `advance_gate`, `ENV_PHASE_ORDER`, `PHASE_ORDER`). Delivers a NEW standalone module `ngv2/fsm_detect.py` with a PURE, deterministic state handler `detect(detect_input: dict) -> dict` that classifies the target's language / build system from a PRE-STAGED filesystem-summary dict (the impure `os.walk` / `web_framework_detect.detect_frameworks` scan is the INJECTED seam, NOT part of this pure leaf — it is supplied as data so the gate is determinism-clean), resolves the ABI interpreter pin (`.python-version` / `pyproject` requires-python string carried in the input), checks eligibility at entry, and emits a content_hash'd `DetectArtifact` dict via `ngv2.fsm_evidence.phase_artifact_hash`. It INHERITS the c0 fail-closed invariant: a `prev_artifact` that is absent / None / `{}` / non-dict / hash-tampered must NOT advance (delegated to `ngv2.fsm_evidence.advance_gate`). Fail-closed typed terminals on its OWN classification: language not in {py,js} -> `no_eligible_language`; no build file present -> `no_build_system`; SHA != pin -> `sha_mismatch`; interpreter pin unresolved -> `interpreter_unresolved`. X-criteria: X1 (a py/js fixture summary advances) + X2 (an ineligible/no-build-file summary is REFUSED with a typed terminal) + X4 (the new state's transition is gated, never auto-advances on absent prior evidence). PARALLEL-SAFE: this child edits ONLY its two NEW files (`ngv2/fsm_detect.py` + its oracle) — DISJOINT from c2 (`ngv2/fsm_provision.py`) and c3 (`ngv2/fsm_jail_build.py`); the live-FSM wiring (inserting `detect` into `PHASE_ORDER`/`worker_phases`/`_TRANSITION_GATES`/`conductor_seams`) is DEFERRED to a single later integration leaf so the three siblings never collide on a shared file. WIRE-UP: `detect` reaches the `python -m ngv2.run_hunt` LIVE_ROOT by CONSUMING the on-live-chain `ngv2.fsm_evidence` (imported by `transition_planner`/`gate_executor`, which `conductor_seams.build_default_seams` imports, which `run_hunt` calls); the deferred integration leaf adds the inbound importer that threads `detect` into the running conductor."
